  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Jemen Peace Support Facility 2019-2022</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Yemen Peace Support Facility 2019-2022 - Yemen Peace Support Facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expected Results
The peace process in Yemen is supported with fast, flexible initiatives, that deliver tangible, rapid improvements in the daily lives of people, and reinforce and build public support for the political process.

Under this output the following components will be implemented (the components have been somewhat altered over the years, but the gist of each window remain):

Component 1: Initiatives emerging from high-level peace consultations or stemming from interactions with the parties

Component 2: Initiatives emerging from existing Track II dialogues

Component 3: Eventual interventions related to the transitional governance arrangement post-deal</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;d till en fredsfond som ska st&#xe4;rka f&#xf6;ruts&#xe4;ttningarna att genomf&#xf6;ra &#xf6;verenskomna steg (genom Stockholmsavtalet, december 2018) mot en fredlig l&#xf6;sning av konflikten i Jemen. Fredsfonden &#xe4;r utformad f&#xf6;r att st&#xf6;dja fredsprocessen med snabba, flexibla initativ som &#xf6;verenskommits av partnerna och som levererar konkreta, snabba f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttringar i m&#xe4;nniskors dagliga liv och f&#xf6;rst&#xe4;rker och bygger offentligt st&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r den politiska processen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to a Peace Support Facility which aims at strenthening the possibilites of the implementation of the Stockholm agreement to enhace the prerequisites for a peaceful solution of the conflict in Yemen. The Facility is designed to support the peace process with fast, flexible initiatives, agreed by the parties, that deliver tangible, rapid improvements in the daily lives of people and reinforce and build public support for the political process.</narrative>
  </description>
